# Testing Guidelines

## Test Structure
- Unit tests are in [tests/](mdc:tests/) directory
- Integration tests are in [integration_tests/](mdc:integration_tests/)
- Use [tests/common.rs](mdc:tests/common.rs) for shared test utilities

## Test Patterns
- Use `#[tokio::test]` for async tests
- Mock external dependencies using the `mocks` feature
- Test error conditions and edge cases
- Verify graceful error handling without task termination

## Reliability Testing
- Test MQTT disconnection and reconnection scenarios
- Verify circuit breaker behavior under failure conditions
- Test channel overflow scenarios
- Validate exponential backoff implementations

## Test Data
- Use fixtures from [integration_tests/fixtures/](mdc:integration_tests/fixtures/)
- Test with realistic packet data from [integration_tests/fixtures/](mdc:integration_tests/fixtures/)
- Verify packet decoding with known good data

## Performance Testing
- Test channel performance under high message volumes
- Verify memory usage patterns
- Test reconnection timing and backoff behavior
